{"shortDescription":"By Avinash  PMost Latin American currencies traded lower on Thursday against the U.S. dollar near multi-week highs, while stocks were mostly higher, with domestic political developments remaining in the spotlight in Brazil.MSCI's index tracking regional stocks (.MILA00000PUS) edged higher by 0.2%.W…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["By Avinash  P"]},{"type":"p","children":["Most Latin American currencies traded lower on Thursday against the U.S. dollar near multi-week highs, while stocks were mostly higher, with domestic political developments remaining in the spotlight in Brazil."]},{"type":"p","children":["MSCI's index tracking regional stocks (.MILA00000PUS) edged higher by 0.2%."]},{"type":"p","children":["With Brazil's presidential elections fast approaching, market focus remained pinned on the contest."]},{"type":"p","children":["An AtlasIntel/Bloomberg poll showed Brazilian Senator Flavio Bolsonaro and President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva remain statistically tied in a simulated runoff ahead of next month's vote."]},{"type":"p","children":["Surveys lately continue to point towards a neck-and-neck race, with market sentiment heavily driven by shifts in electoral odds."]},{"type":"p","children":["Against this backdrop, President Lula announced a 15% increase in cash transfers under the country's flagship welfare program, Bolsa Familia, to shore up his support ahead of the election."]},{"type":"p","children":["The program adds to investor anxiety over the deteriorating public finances under the current government."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"Brazil's most pressing challenge is to sustainably reduce its abnormally high interest rates, which are weighing heavily on the public sector, businesses, and households,\" Barclays analysts said in a note."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"With real rates still near double digits, maintaining the status quo for another four years is unlikely to be viable.\""]},{"type":"p","children":["The benchmark Ibovespa index ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV","text":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV"}}," lost 0.3%, while the real ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDBRL","text":"FX_IDC:USDBRL"}}," inched slightly lower."]},{"type":"p","children":["On the monetary policy front, Brazil's central bank on Wednesday cut interest rates by 25 basis points for a fifth straight meeting amid firmer signs of an economic slowdown while keeping its options open ahead of the election."]},{"type":"p","children":["Across the broader currency space, MSCI's index of Latin American currencies (.MILA00000CUS) fell 0.2%."]},{"type":"p","children":["The U.S. dollar ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TVC:DXY","text":"TVC:DXY"}}," eased slightly after touching seven-week highs, following the Federal Reserve's widely anticipated rate hike to the 3.75% to 4.00% range and policymakers signaling further tightening."]},{"type":"p","children":["Elsewhere in the region, the Mexican peso (=MXN) gained 0.4%, after hitting an over-one-month low of 17.2710 a dollar in the prior session. Mexico's benchmark stock index ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMV:ME","text":"BMV:ME"}}," rose 0.5%, as trading resumed following a holiday on Wednesday."]},{"type":"p","children":["In Argentina, data later in the day is expected to show gross domestic product likely grew 1.6% year-on-year in the second quarter, slowing from growth of 6.5% in the same period of 2025, according to a Reuters poll."]},{"type":"p","children":["Earlier this week, President Javier Milei's government presented its 2027 budget to Congress, forecasting 4% economic growth next year and inflation of 18%, down from 29% this year."]},{"type":"p","children":["Local stocks ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BCBA:IMV","text":"BCBA:IMV"}}," advanced 0.8%."]},{"type":"p","children":["MSCI's Chilean stock index (.MICL00000PUS) rose 0.5%, supported by firmer copper prices, as the country is a major exporter of the metal. The support from higher metal prices also helped cushion the peso's ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDCLP","text":"FX_IDC:USDCLP"}}," fall against the dollar, down 0.3%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Key Latin American stock indexes and currencies at 1457 GMT:"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Latin American market prices from Reuters"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Equities"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Latest"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Daily % change"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["MSCI Emerging Markets ","CBOE:EFS"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["1688.31"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["0.1"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["MSCI LatAm (.MILA00000PUS)"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["3100.7"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["0.15"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Brazil Bovespa ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV","text":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV"}}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["185045.89"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["-0.27"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Mexico IPC ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMV:ME","text":"BMV:ME"}}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","childre